# The Rust build tree, the schemas `tauri-build` regenerates on every build, and
# the window config `desktop:sync` writes from the environment. None of the three
# is anyone's to review.
dist/
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
src-tauri/tauri.conf.gen.json

# Cargo resolves this from Cargo.toml on first build. A committed one would be
# 4,600 machine-written lines in a repo that caps a reviewable file at 300, and
# nothing in CI compiles this crate, so there is no build for it to pin. The
# cost is stated under "What is deliberately not wired" in README.md.
src-tauri/Cargo.lock
